From ecad3177941b275d52dc1f2273a5a51c3fe38b84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cameron Baird <cameronbaird@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:55:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pathrs: tolerate dot-separated kernel localversions

Pathrs parses the uname release when selecting safe procfs operations.
MSHV releases such as 6.6.137.mshv2-2.azl3 leave a trailing dot in the
numeric prefix, causing host_kernel_version to panic.

Strip one dot before an alphabetic localversion while preserving
malformed bare trailing-dot versions, and update the Cargo vendor
checksum.

Signed-off-by: Cameron Baird <cameronbaird@microsoft.com>
---
 vendor/pathrs/.cargo-checksum.json        |  2 +-
 vendor/pathrs/src/utils/kernel_version.rs | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vendor/pathrs/.cargo-checksum.json b/vendor/pathrs/.cargo-checksum.json
index 5fb9056..9d8ac84 100644
--- a/vendor/pathrs/.cargo-checksum.json
+++ b/vendor/pathrs/.cargo-checksum.json
@@ -1 +1 @@
